<title>FINLAND: NOKIA SEEN TESTING 200 MARKKA IN BULLISH HELSINKI.</title>
<headline>NOKIA SEEN TESTING 200 MARKKA IN BULLISH HELSINKI.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bourse sentiment was encouraged</p>
<p>by Wall Street's second consecutive record close and Nokia,</p>
<p>which closed near 200 markka, there was seen testing it in</p>
<p>Helsinki on Tuesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Nokia is likely to test that level ... if it breaks it,</p>
<p>things look good,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>Another noted, however, that the share is normally priced in</p>
<p>New York, and added that Finnish investors may not be keen to</p>
<p>test the level in fear of a rebound there later.</p>
<p>Forestries were also expected to be in focus after strong</p>
<p>gains in U.S. paper stocks.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
